NO REDISTRIBUTED THIRD-PARTY CONTENT

The unit list in `examples/` is derived from a synthetic case study carried in
the authors' own private tree -- a fictional organisational-health report
authored on 2026-04-14 as a fixture for a document-extraction pipeline, whose
figures have no real-world referent. No number here is a fact about a real
organisation and the reporting lines are invented in full: the source carried
none, which is the first thing this audit reports about it.

NO PERSON IS NAMED. Officers appear by ROLE. The fixture's own executive labels
carried person-shaped names, and although they were synthetic, a common name
published beside a performance rating and an adverse finding reads as a record
about somebody whether or not it is one. Nothing in the audit keys on those
labels -- it matches on the unit identifier -- so the names cost nothing to
remove and are not here.

`battery/make_series.py` generates capture series and they are not committed.
They exist to measure where each axiom arm starts answering, which is a fact
about the engine; a finding produced by a generated series is never evidence
about an organisation, and `docs/burn-in.md` says so where the numbers are.

